            <h1>Aluminium vs Tinplate Aerosol Cans: Cost, Performance & Manufacturing Comparison</h1>

            <p>Selecting the correct aerosol can material is a foundational engineering decision that affects product safety, long-term stability, regulatory compliance, manufacturing efficiency, and overall cost structure. Aluminium and tinplate (steel) are the two dominant materials used globally for aerosol packaging, each backed by decades of industrial use and well-established standards.</p>

            <p>This article provides a fact-based, technically accurate comparison of aluminium and tinplate aerosol cans, focusing on manufacturing processes, mechanical performance, corrosion behavior, cost structures, and practical selection criteria, with relevance for startups, students, and entrepreneurs operating in India and global markets.</p>

