            <section id="why-selection-matters">
                <h2>Why Aerosol Can Material Selection Matters</h2>
                <p>Aerosol cans are pressure vessels that must safely contain liquefied or compressed propellants, maintain formulation stability for years, and remain compatible with automated high-speed filling lines. The choice of can material directly influences pressure tolerance, internal coating requirements, transport economics, and recyclability.</p>
                <p>An incorrect material choice can lead to corrosion failures, deformation, valve leakage, or regulatory non-compliance—issues that often surface only after products reach the market, when remediation is costly.</p>

                <h3>Key implications of can material selection include:</h3>
                <div class="table-responsive">
                    <table>
