            <section id="faq">
                <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                
                <h3>Are aluminium aerosol cans safer than tinplate cans?</h3>
                <p>Both materials are safe when correctly designed, coated, and tested to applicable aerosol standards. Safety depends on engineering and quality control, not material alone.</p>
                
                <h3>Which aerosol can material is cheaper in India?</h3>
                <p>Tinplate cans are generally cheaper per unit in India due to local steel availability, but total cost depends on volume, transport, and application.</p>
                
                <h3>Can the same filling line be used for aluminium and tinplate cans?</h3>
                <p>Yes, with proper changeovers and crimp adjustments, most modern filling lines can handle both can types.</p>
                
                <h3>Which material offers better shelf life?</h3>
                <p>Shelf life depends more on internal coatings and formulation compatibility than on the base metal itself.</p>
